<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Dogali</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1887">1887</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Dogali was fought on 26 January 1887 near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/massawa">Massawa</a>, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-sea">Red Sea</a> coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eritrea">Eritrea</a>, when an Ethiopian army under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ras">Ras</a> Alula destroyed an Italian column of some 500 men marching to relieve a besieged fort. The defeat shocked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> and briefly checked its expansion inland from Massawa.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-dogali.jpg" alt="Battle of Dogali" width="320" height="195" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Michele Cammarano · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bataille_de_Dogali.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
